- Use the direct non-pooled Neon URL for migrations/schema setup; pooled PgBouncer URLs can behave badly for migration tools.
- Increase both connection timeout and query/statement timeout in the client or ORM.
- If previews need to be instantly responsive, disable or lengthen Neon scale-to-zero for the preview compute, or explicitly warm it before routing traffic.
- Do not assume the Neon API “branch created” response means “ready for first query.”

Neon’s own docs call out latency/timeouts from scale-to-zero and recommend timeout handling or adjusting suspend settings: https://neon.com/docs/connect/connection-latency

