- `clearInterval(...)` prevents the timer leak.
- You also need to unsubscribe/close the WebSocket, otherwise it can continue receiving events after unmount.
- If you use `addEventListener`, cleanup should call `removeEventListener` with the same handler reference.
- If the effect depends on props/state, make sure the dependency array is correct so old sockets are cleaned up before new ones are created.
- Guard against setting state after unmount if async callbacks can fire during close/reconnect logic.

So: if your cleanup only clears the interval, the WebSocket cleanup is probably incomplete.

