With Inertia SSR off, `<Head>` is only applied after the JS app hydrates. So it will show in DevTools/client-side DOM, but not in “View Page Source” or the initial HTML response. Crawlers that rely on the first response may miss it.

For crawler-critical directives like `noindex`, put them server-side:

```blade
{{-- resources/views/app.blade.php --}}
@if($noindex ?? false)
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
@endif
```

Or better for sensitive/non-indexable routes, send an HTTP header:

```php
return Inertia::render('Private/Page')
    ->toResponse($request)
    ->withHeaders([
        'X-Robots-Tag' => 'noindex, nofollow',
    ]);
```

Use Inertia `<Head>` for normal titles/descriptions where client rendering is acceptable, but use Blade or `X-Robots-Tag` for anything crawlers must see reliably. Re-enable Inertia SSR only if you need the whole page head/body rendered into the initial HTML.

